5. SUB-PRODUCT IDENTIFICATION & POPULATION RULES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SCANNING RULE — SEARCH THE ENTIRE DOCUMENT:
Do NOT limit sub-product extraction to sections explicitly headed "Electronic Banking"
or similar. Scan ALL clauses, bullet points, and sub-clauses throughout the entire
document including general Bank Mandate sections, Common Powers, and Annexes,
and apply the two-gate test to each one individually.

A clause is ONLY extracted as a Sub-Product if it passes BOTH gates:

GATE 1 — The clause must explicitly contain at least one of these terms:
  • internet banking facilities / internet banking
  • electronic banking facilities / electronic banking
  • electronic banking platforms / electronic platforms
  • System Administrator(s)
  • online banking profile
  • E-banking / HSBCnet / H2H / API's
  • Channels / E-Channels (in a digital context)
  • authorisation levels (on a digital platform)
  • third parties to manage Channels
  • electronic banking systems / connectivity channels
  • user access (in context of banking platforms)
  • login PIN / token administration

  IMPORTANT: Any clause containing the phrase "internet banking" or
  "electronic banking" in ANY form automatically passes Gate 1,
  regardless of the section it appears in.

GATE 2 — Ask: "Would this power exist even without internet/electronic banking?"
  If YES → REJECT. It is a general banking power.
  If NO  → ACCEPT. It is genuinely electronic banking-specific.

Step 1 — Link qualifying sub-products to each Account Number from Section 4.
Step 2 — Each qualifying sub-product gets its own object in the "Sub-Products"
          array with its own "Signing Rule" array.
If no clauses pass both gates, set "Sub-Products": []
